Exact meaningful update: ComfyUI v0.36.0 released 2026-09-18;
surfaced/confirmed this scan. The release adds native open-source support
for FastVideo FastH3. FastVideo=E2=80=99s underlying FastH3 8-Step V2 was r=
eleased
2026-09-15: an eight-forward, data-free DMD2-distilled MiniMax-H3
checkpoint using 80% Video Sparse Attention.

Why this clears the bar: FastH3 was already interesting, but native ComfyUI
support materially changes integration cost. We no longer need to depend on
fragile third-party attention-patching nodes to get accelerated
native-audio H3 generation into the production graph. This is exactly the
kind of =E2=80=98research becomes practical primitive=E2=80=99 transition t=
he scanner
should catch.

Inputs -> outputs: text or image conditioning -> synchronized generated
video + native audio. FastH3 is intended as the accelerated MiniMax-H3
generation path.

Code / weights: ComfyUI and FastVideo are open source; FastVideo code is
Apache-2.0. FastH3 derives from MiniMax-H3, so model/output commercial and
territorial restrictions from the MiniMax-H3 Community License still need
to be respected; do not infer Apache-2.0 from the runtime onto the model
weights.

Hardware/performance: FastVideo=E2=80=99s FastH3 family is sparse/distilled
specifically to reduce generation compute. Earlier community ports
demonstrated watchable 4-step drafts on 24 GB consumer cards, but v0.36=E2=
=80=99s
native integration should be benchmarked directly rather than assuming
those third-party numbers transfer. FastVideo=E2=80=99s 8-Step V2 uses 80% =
Video
Sparse Attention.

Maturity: RUNNABLE / moving toward PRODUCTIONISH.

Relevance: high for AI hosts, B-roll, generated scenes and audiovisual
inserts. This is more important for our premium/source-performance renderer
than for real-time talking avatars.

Exact experiment: pin ComfyUI v0.36.0 and generate the same 10 canonical
host/B-roll prompts through (A) native FastH3 8-Step V2, (B) dense
MiniMax-H3, and =C2=A9 our current premium renderer. Record wall time, peak
VRAM, identity score, lip/audio sync, temporal stability, usable-clip rate
and $/usable second. Then run the winner through Hypit/Content Machine
rather than generating variants stochastically.

Replacement/complement: retire experimental FastH3 custom-node glue where
native ComfyUI now covers the same path. Keep VDN-H3 as a separate
long-context candidate and LTX-2.3 MSR for multi-subject scenes.
TOP 5 TO TEST RIGHT NOW

   1. Native ComfyUI 0.36 FastH3 benchmark.
   2. Hypit 20-variant deterministic-edit benchmark.
   3. Content Machine Production Run Ledger / feedback-loop benchmark.
   4. LTX-2.3 MSR two-character scene benchmark.
   5. Identity-QA across all renderers.

BEST OPEN-SOURCE AI INFLUENCER STACK

Character Asset Graph + canonical identity embedding -> persona/memory ->
showrunner/acting policy -> Performance IR + Live Cue Timeline -> cheap
browser/edge avatar for drafts/live -> native ComfyUI FastH3 / LTX-MSR /
other premium stochastic renderer for source performances ->
identity/lipsync critic -> Production Run Ledger -> Hypit/Content Machine
-> HyperFrames/OpenShorts deterministic edit/render -> publish -> platform
metrics -> Style/Profile Library.
BIGGEST CAPABILITY JUMP

Accelerated audiovisual generation is becoming a first-class ComfyUI
primitive instead of research-specific glue. The important delta is
integration reliability and interchangeability, not a new foundation model.
CHEAPEST PRACTICAL WIN

Delete custom acceleration glue where ComfyUI v0.36 now provides the
supported FastH3 path; spend engineering time on evaluation, identity QA
and production feedback instead.
WATCH NEXT

